  "description": "Simple and lightweight brute force protection for .NET 10.\n      This library will protect defined actions in your MVC controllers, Minimal API endpoints, and Razor Pages by making them inefficient to be brute-forced.\n  \n      It will append request times in milliseconds if a local cache entry on the server is found for the same request, \n      request name, and method, and the hit count reaches a defined limit (referred to here as \"green requests\") within a specified amount of time.",
  "id": "NoBrute",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-08-01T03:38:27.427Z",
  "licenseFile": "LICENSE",
  "licenseUrl": "https://aka.ms/deprecateLicenseUrl",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "M8B1x8l3bhCh1YUMsBLmY+S/LF1Yjo/0H6gse7FqCsLOZVsd2aRKgZA8yBePOrTy2a+ssdws70YijSKfRlFXLA==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 43608,
  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/nfMalde/NoBrute",
  "published": "2026-08-01T03:35:48.48Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.MD",
  "releaseNotes": "* Fully asynchronous request pipeline: no Thread.Sleep and no blocking cache calls anymore, so bot waves can no longer starve the thread pool\n      * Added CheckRequestAsync / ReleaseRequestAsync / AutoProcessRequestReleaseAsync (existing custom INoBrute implementations keep working)\n      * Added support for reverse proxies (Cloudflare, load balancers) via CF-Connecting-IP / X-Forwarded-For with trusted proxies and networks\n      * Added a global circuit breaker (MaxTrackedEntries) that hard blocks new clients instead of flooding the cache\n      * Cache entries now expire after TimeUntilReset instead of living forever\n      * Added MaxIncreaseRequestTime to cap the delay of a single request",
